    "q-341994": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341994",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $0.6$ | $0.9$ | $1.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $-2.7$ | $-1.6$ | $-0.4$ | $1.1$ | $3.7$ |\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=0.6$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${g}^{′}(0.6)≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=0.6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.3.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(0.6) & ≈\\frac{g(0.6+0.3)-g(0.6)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(0.9)-g(0.6)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.1-(-0.4)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{0.3} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
