    "q-71917": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71917",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A function $F(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $3.5$ | $8.7$ | $11.2$ | $12.9$ | $6.7$ | $1.2$ |\n\nApproximate ${F}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=2$ using a forward difference approximation.",
      "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{F(x+h)-F(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{F(2+2)-F(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{F(4)-F(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{11.2-8.7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.5}{2} \\\\  & =1.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
