    "q-342003": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342003",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "A function $d(y)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $d(y)$ | $-8.92$ | $-11.34$ | $-15.23$ | $-17.56$ | $-18.21$ | $-18.50$ |\n\nApproximate ${d}^{′}(y)$ at the point $y=-5$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${d}^{′}(-5)≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{d}^{′}(y)≈\\frac{d(y+h)-d(y)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $y=-5.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}^{′}(-5) & ≈\\frac{d(-5+2)-d(-5)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{d(-3)-d(-5)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-11.34-(-8.92)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2.42}{2} \\\\  & =-1.21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
          "dom_index": 0,
          "disabled": false,
          "input_html": "<div id=\"freeResponseTextbox-1\" class=\"matheditor-wrapper-answer\" ;=\"\" style=\"min-width:50px;\n                                        margin-left:2px;\n                                        margin-right:4px;\n                                        background:;\"><div class=\"mq-editable-field mq-math-mode\" style=\"border: none; outline: none;\"><span class=\"mq-textarea\"><textarea autocapitalize=\"off\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\"true\" style=\"\" disabled=\"\"></textarea></span><span class=\"mq-root-block\" mathquill-block-id=\"7\"><span mathquill-command-id=\"9\" class=\"\">−</span><span mathquill-command-id=\"11\">1</span><span mathquill-command-id=\"13\">.</span><span mathquill-command-id=\"15\">2</span><span mathquill-command-id=\"17\">1</span></span></div></div>",
