    "q-71926": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71926",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "A shepherd keeps track of the rate of growth of his herd. He takes note of the total number of sheep every $6$ months. The results are shown in the table below, where $S(m)$ is the number of sheep after $m$ months.\n\n| $m$ | $6$ | $12$ | $18$ | $24$ | $30$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $S(m)$ | $90$ | $98$ | $116$ | $130$ | $139$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of growth of the herd at the point where $m=12$ using a forward difference approximation.",
      "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{S}^{′}(m)≈\\frac{S(m+h)-S(m)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $m=6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=6.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(12) & ≈\\frac{S(12+6)-S(12)}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{S(18)-S(12)}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{116-98}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{6} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, at $m=12$ the rate of growth is approximately $3\\,\\text{sheep/month}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-71926-a",
