    "q-342046": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342046",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "The weight of a radioactive substance was recorded over time for $15$ seconds. The following table shows the weight $M(t)$, in grams, recorded at time $t$ in seconds.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ | $12$ | $15$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $M(t)$ | $8.0$ | $7.1$ | $6.3$ | $5.4$ | $4.8$ | $4.1$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of weight at time $t=6$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the weight decreases.\n\nAt $t=6,$ the estimated rate of change is {{field-1}} grams per second.",
      "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{M(t+h)-M(t)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $t=6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=3.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}^{′}(6) & ≈\\frac{M(6+3)-M(6)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M(9)-M(6)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5.4-6.3}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-0.9}{3} \\\\  & =-0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, at $t=6$ the rate of change was approximately $-0.3$ grams per second.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
