    },
    "q-342080": {
      "dom_id": "step-q342080",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14190413/assets/ae57faa04abd053e4a58d751cc084d58e07e84e0520c99a33a122f58dfd8f18c.png)\n\nA slice of jackfruit is placed in an air dryer. The graph of the moisture content $M(t)$, in percent, after $t$ hours is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the moisture content at $t=3$ using a forward difference with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the content decreases.\n\nAfter $3$ hour, the rate of change of moisture content is {{field-1}} percent per hour.",
      "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{M(t+h)-M(t)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{M(3+2)-M(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M(5)-M(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{20-40}{2} \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $3$ hour, the rate of change of moisture content is $-10$ percent per hour.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
