      "dom_id": "step-q51400",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14190413/assets/e3f8c906203c565cf3b1accf2aa03f6bdb9a06c064283bf9b6383153ec35b837.png)\n\nAn object is changing in size. The graph of its volume $V(t),$ in cubic centimeters, after $t$ minutes is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the object's volume's at $t=3$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{V}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{V(t+h)-V(t)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{V(3+1)-V(3)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{V(4)-V(3)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-3}{1} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $3$ minutes, the volume changes at a rate of approximately $-1\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}/\\text{min}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
